{"id":"3db0e645-0c25-4fd3-b0e0-c817236021d9","object":"chat.completion","created":1793847464,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I'll inspect the new environ.py class body, then apply the remaining two file edits, fix the config error message to name the variable, run pytest, and write run.log/patch.diff.\n\n```python\nenv_r = read_file('deepinfer/environ.py')\nenv = env_r['content']\nprint('hash', env_r['file_hash'], 'len', len(env))\ni = env.find('class EnvVar')\nprint(env[max(0, i - 400):i + 2600])\nprint('---- config block ----')\nk = env.find('DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS')\nprint(env[max(0, k - 700):k + 500])\n```\n\nFix the factory to include the variable name in its ValueError, then extend the formatter and mark stats messages.\n\n```python\nr1 = replace_text_batch('deepinfer/environ.py', [\n    {'old_text': '''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none_ge(*, minimum: int) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        \"\"\"Optional int parsed with ``int``; unset stays None, values below ``minimum`` are rejected.\"\"\"\n\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            value = int(v)\n            if value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{v!r} must be >= {minimum}\")\n            return value\n\n        return EnvVar(_init)''',\n     'new_text': '''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none_ge(*, minimum: int, name: str):\n        \"\"\"可选整数配置：未设置时为 None；设置时用 int 解析且不得小于 minimum。\"\"\"\n\n        def _init(v: str | None):\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            try:\n                value = int(v)\n            except (TypeError, ValueError) as exc:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"{name} must be an integer >= {minimum}, got {v!r}\"\n                ) from exc\n            if value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be an integer >= {minimum}, got {v!r}\")\n            return value\n\n        return EnvVar(_init)'''},\n    {'old_text': '    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_ge(minimum=32)',\n     'new_text': '    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_ge(\\n        minimum=32, name=\"DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\"\\n    )'},\n], env_r['file_hash'])\nprint(r1)\n\nlg = read_file('deepinfer/logger.py')\nr2 = replace_text_batch('deepinfer/logger.py', [\n    {'old_text': '''_DATE_FORMAT = \"%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"''',\n     'new_text': '''_DATE_FORMAT = \"%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"\n_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS = 32\n_OMITTED_MARK = \"...<omitted>...\"'''},\n    {'old_text': '''        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n\n    def formatTime(self, record: logging.LogRecord, datefmt: str | None = None) -> str:''',\n     'new_text': '''        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= {_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS} or None, \"\n                    f\"got {max_message_chars!r}\"\n                )\n            if max_message_chars < _MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS:\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= {_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS} or None, \"\n                    f\"got {max_message_chars!r}\"\n                )\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n\n    def _truncate_message(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str | None:\n        \"\"\"返回截断后的消息正文；无需截断时返回 None（不改动 record）。\"\"\"\n        budget = self.max_message_chars\n        if budget is None:\n            return None\n        if getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            return None\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if len(message) <= budget:\n            return None\n        mark = _OMITTED_MARK\n        remaining = budget - len(mark)\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            return message[:budget]\n        head = -(-remaining // 2)\n        tail = remaining - head\n        head_part = message[:head]\n        tail_part = message[len(message) - tail :] if tail > 0 else \"\"\n        return f\"{head_part}{mark}{tail_part}\"\n\n    def formatTime(self, record: logging.LogRecord, datefmt: str | None = None) -> str:'''},\n    {'old_text': '''    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)''',\n     'new_text': '''    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        truncated = self._truncate_message(record)\n        if truncated is not None:\n            # 复制记录后再格式化，避免改写共享原记录的 msg/args/message\n            record = logging.makeLogRecord(dict(record.__dict__))\n            record.msg = truncated\n            record.args = None\n        msg = super().format(record)'''},\n    {'old_text': '''    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n    )''',\n     'new_text': '''    from deepinfer.environ import envs\n\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )'''},\n], lg['file_hash'])\nprint(r2)\n\nsl = read_file('deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py')\nr3 = replace_text_batch('deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py', [\n    {'old_text': '''            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)''',\n     'new_text': '''            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})'''},\n], sl['file_hash'])\nprint(r3)\n\ntest = run_command(['python', '-m', 'pytest', '-q'], '.')\nprint(test['rc'])\nprint(test['stdout'][-4000:])\n```\n```\n\n```python\nimport json\nlog = \"==== command: python -m pytest -q ====\\nrc=%s\\n\" % test['rc'] + test['stdout'] + \"\\n\" + (test.get('stderr') or '')\ndc = run_command(['git', 'diff', '--', 'deepinfer/environ.py', 'deepinfer/logger.py', 'deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py'], '.')\ndiff = dc['stdout']\nif not diff.strip():\n    dc = run_command(['git', 'diff', 'HEAD', '--', 'deepinfer/environ.py', 'deepinfer/logger.py', 'deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py'], '.')\n    diff = dc['stdout']\nprint('diff rc', dc['rc'], 'len', len(diff))\nfor name, text in [('run.log', log), ('patch.diff', diff)]:\n    for h in ['', '0' * 64]:\n        try:\n            print(write_file(name, text, h))\n            break\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(name, 'err', e)\nif test['rc'] == 0:\n    print(final_answer({'status': 'ok', 'pytest': 'all passed', 'files': ['deepinfer/environ.py', 'deepinfer/logger.py', 'deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py']}))\n```\n```","reasoning_content":"I need to apply logger.py and stats_logger.py edits now, plus verify. Requests left: 1 after this response. Need to be efficient: do edits, run pytest, generate run.log and patch.diff, and final_answer in one action ideally.\n\nLet me first read the current environ.py to check my edit is valid (I need to see whether EnvVar.int_or_none_ge fits the existing class - the class may not be generic subscriptable). Wait — my earlier edit added `-> EnvVar[int | None]` which may fail if EnvVar isn't generic. And the old_text matched, so ok=True. I need to check the environ.py content around the edit.\n\nBut I have limited requests (1 left). Let me do everything in a single action: read environ.py relevant sections, print, then write logger.py and stats_logger.py edits, run pytest, write run.log and patch.diff.\n\nBut I can't see environ.py before writing logger edits... I can do it all in one block with condi